From 4395de46a27c19391b20325757e78f2247ac662c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Tong <zhengtong0611@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 8 Nov 2026 07:24:20 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 12/12] Credits: Mate Engine, the Linux port, community dances;
 say what this fork is

The top-level README gets a short note about this fork (debate referee and
side bots, for whack-2026) that keeps upstream attribution and the
MateEngine Pro License terms. The Referee README now credits
Marksonthegamer's Linux port and the community dance creators, and says
the dances are not redistributed.
---
 Assets/MATE ENGINE - Referee/README.md | 13 +++++++++++--
 README.md                              | 19 +++++++++++++++++++
 2 files changed, 30 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/Assets/MATE ENGINE - Referee/README.md b/Assets/MATE ENGINE - Referee/README.md
index 9dc834f..d18582a 100644
--- a/Assets/MATE ENGINE - Referee/README.md	
+++ b/Assets/MATE ENGINE - Referee/README.md	
@@ -323,8 +323,10 @@ no-rebuild fallback). No scene, prefab or project setting is changed: everything
 ## Licence and credits
 
 - **Mate Engine**
-  - This fork, including these additions, is a derivative of Mate Engine by Shiny and is distributed under the
-    **MateEngine Pro License v2.0** (see `LICENSE`).
+  - This fork, including these additions, is a derivative of [Mate Engine](https://github.com/shinyflvre/Mate-Engine)
+    by shinyflvre (Shiny / Johnson Jason) and contributors, by way of the unofficial
+    [Linux port](https://github.com/Marksonthegamer/Mate-Engine-Linux-Port) by Marksonthegamer. It is distributed
+    under the **MateEngine Pro License v2.0** (see `LICENSE`).
   - The source stays public, attribution must be kept, and commercial use is not allowed.
   - The components required to build and run this version (this folder, the build script and the mock server)
     are included.
@@ -339,3 +341,10 @@ no-rebuild fallback). No scene, prefab or project setting is changed: everything
   - No code from maoxig's separate CustomDancePlayer repository is used: it has no licence.
 - **Third-party packages** are unchanged from upstream; see `Third Party Licenses/`.
 - **Programs that talk to the bridge** use only the HTTP protocol above. They contain no Mate Engine code.
+- **Community dances.** The verdict dances (`tools/mate-bots.sh` copies "MMD-Conqueror", "MMD-Lost One_s Weeping" and
+  "MMD-皆大欢喜-卜逻desu" into a local build) come from the Mate Engine community's CustomDances collection. The
+  motions and music belong to their creators: the original MMD motion and song authors, and the collection's
+  contributors (folders such as Yongqisang and Xenophn). They are **not** included in this repository or any build we
+  publish. Get them from that collection and point `DANCE_LIBRARY` at it.
+- **Made for** whack-2026 ([JollyPerson/whack-2026](https://github.com/JollyPerson/whack-2026)), the debate server
+  these channels talk to.
diff --git a/README.md b/README.md
index 82f41cd..53e3e35 100755
--- a/README.md
+++ b/README.md
@@ -1,3 +1,22 @@
+# Mate-Engine-Linux-Port: debate referee and side-bot fork
+
+> [!NOTE]
+> This is a fork made for **whack-2026**, a live debate fact-checker
+> ([JollyPerson/whack-2026](https://github.com/JollyPerson/whack-2026)). Branch `side-bots` adds a speech bridge, so
+> Mate Engine avatars can show the debate server's lines in speech bubbles. It also adds two side-bot avatars (For
+> and Against), verdict dances with music on or off and an automatic stop, a command-line build and dance export, and
+> the launcher `tools/mate-bots.sh`. Details, the wire protocol and credits are in
+> [`Assets/MATE ENGINE - Referee/README.md`](Assets/MATE%20ENGINE%20-%20Referee/README.md).
+>
+> **Credits.** [Mate Engine](https://github.com/shinyflvre/Mate-Engine) is by shinyflvre (Shiny / Johnson Jason) and
+> contributors. The Linux port this fork is based on, [Mate-Engine-Linux-Port](https://github.com/Marksonthegamer/Mate-Engine-Linux-Port),
+> is by Marksonthegamer. Everything here, the fork's additions included, is distributed under the
+> **MateEngine Pro License v2.0** (`LICENSE`): free of charge, non-commercial, source public, attribution kept.
+> This fork is not affiliated with or endorsed by the Mate Engine project or the Linux port's author.
+> The upstream README follows unchanged.
+
+---
